## Title

sparse_rc move constructor reads uninitialized nr_/nc_/nnz_ before swap

## Body

### Summary

`CppAD::sparse_rc<SizeVector>::sparse_rc(sparse_rc&&)` has no member-initializer
list and immediately calls `swap(other)`. That reads indeterminate `nr_`, `nc_`,
and `nnz_` via `std::swap`. GCC 14 at `-O2` reports this as `-Wuninitialized`
(often attributed to `bits/move.h`).

### Location

`include/cppad/utility/sparse_rc.hpp`:

```cpp
sparse_rc(sparse_rc&& other)
{  swap(other); }
```

### Suggested fix

Match the pattern already used by `CppAD::vector`:

```cpp
sparse_rc(sparse_rc&& other)
: nr_(0), nc_(0), nnz_(0)
{  swap(other); }
```

`sparse_rcv`'s move constructor is fine: its `swap` only exchanges already-
constructed class members.

### How it shows up

Compiling an R package that move-constructs a type containing a `sparse_rc`
member (e.g. via an implicit move constructor) with Rtools45 / GCC 14.3
`-O2 -Wall` produces:

```
bits/move.h:234:11: warning: '...' is used uninitialized [-Wuninitialized]
  inlined from sparse_rc::swap
  inlined from sparse_rc(sparse_rc&&)
```

### Environment

- CppAD 20260000.0
- g++ (GCC) 14.3.0 (x86_64-w64-mingw32, Rtools45)

